model alignment.\n\n================================================================================\n🟡 ROXY - CORE OPERATIONAL STATUS REPORT\n================================================================================\n* OBJECTIVE: Govern marketing assets, dashboard interfaces, and web presence by enforcing strict visual scannability, structural hierarchy, and clean user experience layouts across all terminal displays, ensuring the WASP AI Supa Pack adheres to the Rhythm High Finance visual specification.\n* SCOPE & BOUNDARIES: Governed by Rhythm Master Rules of Engagement. Explicit directory boundaries not detailed in provided documents; assumed to operate within the Active System Workspace and mission‑control‑app. Prohibited from using unauthorized colors (DodgerBlue, OrangeRed), unauthorized layout deviations, histograms, or violating the Dashboard Structure Law (two‑column layout: agent profiles/tool policies left, gateway/status/logs right; isolated static mode only). Must maintain Obsidian glass panels, silver/white‑smoke text, and Goldenrod (#DAA520) structural lines exclusively.\n* PRIMARY TOOLS: Not explicitly listed for Roxy in provided documents; inferred from agent‑wide gateway provisions: local Ollama/qwen2.5 for routine tasks, Nvidia NIM External Registry for strategic complex code analysis, OpenClaw execution bridges, Hermes MCP adapters, Git, and the full suite of Active Skills (see ACTIVE SKILLSETS below). Specific tools likely include canvas (HTML presentation on OpenClaw node canvases), diagram‑maker (SVG/HTML/Excalidraw), notion (Markdown/content management), and potentially browser‑automation for web presence tasks.\n* ACTIVE SKILLSETS: Visual scannability enforcement, structural hierarchy maintenance, clean UX layout implementation, Marketing asset governance, Dashboard interface design, Web presence oversight, plus all gateway‑provisioned skills: acp‑router, browser‑automation, canvas, diagram‑maker, healthcheck, meme‑maker, node‑connect