law execution bridges, Hermes MCP adapters, Git, and the full suite of Active Skills (see ACTIVE SKILLSETS below). Likely includes npm, pip, and local Ollama/qwen2.5 for routine tasks, Nvidia NIM for strategic complex analysis.\n* ACTIVE SKILLSETS: Localized server bridge management, WebSocket connection handling, Node.js runtime supervision, backend infrastructure maintenance, inter‑agent communication facilitation, real‑time data streaming support, plus all gateway‑provisioned skills: acp‑router, browser‑automation, canvas, diagram‑maker, healthcheck, meme‑maker, node‑connect, node‑inspect‑debugger, notion, python‑debugpy, skill‑creator, spike, taskflow, taskflow‑inbox‑triage, video‑frames, weather.\n* MISSION UNDERSTANDING: Jack provides the connective tissue that binds Charlie’s algorithmic outputs, Tess’s risk triggers, and Roxy’s UI presentations into a cohesive, real‑time operational system. By maintaining stable WebSocket links and Node.js services, he ensures low‑latency data flow from exchange listeners (via Active Exchange API Listeners mapped in TOOLS.md) to execution engines, while preserving the offline‑first, sovereign mandate through local hardware binding and strict adherence to the Rhythm Master Rules. His infrastructure enables the closed‑loop autonomy that defines the WASP AI Supa Pack’s high‑velocity, zero‑dependency execution model.\n\n================================================================================\n🟡 SILAS - CORE OPERATIONAL STATUS REPORT\n================================================================================\n* OBJECTIVE: No explicit information found in provided documents (AGENTS.md, SOUL.md, IDENTITY.md, MEMORY.md, HEARTBEAT.md, AUDIT_REPORT.md, TOOLS.md, or workspace files) regarding a Director named Silas or a role titled “Database Architecture & State Retention.”\n* SCOPE & BOUNDARIES: Undocumented in available sources; cannot specify authorized directories, banned actions, or governance boundaries without expl