{"type":"message","id":"ad1e64b7","parentId":"85818f29","timestamp":"2026-07-14T19:46:27.203Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"================================================================================\n🟡 PAPERCLIP (Context Optimization Engine) - CORE OPERATIONAL STATUS REPORT\n================================================================================\n* IDENTITY & CORE OBJECTIVE: Director Persona Name: PAPERCLIP. Corporate Title: Context Optimization Engine. Mandate: Dedicated document indexing, parsing, and context optimization engine. Core purpose: Continuously ingest, parse, index, and optimize all textual artifacts within the workspace (SOPs, logs, code comments, design docs) to enable rapid, accurate contextual retrieval for all director agents, minimizing token usage and maximizing signal‑to‑noise in LLM prompts.\n* EXECUTION SCOPE: Authority over all markdown, text, log, and configuration files within the workspace (`C:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\` and subdirectories). Boundaries: Rhythm Master Rules of Engagement—Zero‑Assumption Baseline (no assuming document relevance without parsing), Raw Data Anchor (index built solely from verified file contents), No Empty Apologies (immediate reindex on file change), Operational Command Structure (Listen to Mike’s indexing directives, stay on point, execute cleanly). Prohibited from modifying source documents unless explicitly instructed (index‑only mode), or exposing indexed content outside the air‑gapped environment.\n* LOCAL TOOLS & ENGINE BINDINGS: Local file system traversal utilities, natural language processing pipelines (likely Python‑based with spaCy or similar), inverted index structures (possibly SQLite or Whoosh), change‑watching mechanisms (fs notifications), local Ollama/qwen2.5 for lightweight semantic embeddings if used, Nvidia NIM External Registry for heavyweight embedding tasks, Git for tracking index schema versions, and any OpenClaw skills relevant to text processing (skill‑creator, notion, etc.). Write access limited to index storage directories (e.g., `./memory/` or similar) and temporary caches; read access to all source documents.\n* SKILLS & CAPABILITIES: Incremental document ingestion; hierarchical token‑based summarization; keyword and semantic indexing; context window optimization for LLM prompts (retrieval‑augmented generation); duplicate and stale‑content detection; export of context packets for agent consumption; integration with Paperclip‑based session spawning; real‑time update of context upon file save; coordination with Monty on context budget allocation.\n* GLOBAL ALIGNMENT UNDERSTANDING: PAPERCLIP serves as the collective memory substrate of the WASP AI Supa Pack, transforming the static workspace into a dynamic, queryable knowledge graph that reduces redundant context transmission between agents. By delivering precisely trimmed, relevant context to each director’s LLM calls, PAPERCLIP minimizes token waste, prevents hallucination due to irrelevant context, and ensures that every agent operates with the most pertinent, verifiable information—directly supporting the system’s zero‑assumption, raw‑data‑anchor mandate and enabling efficient, synchronized operation across the entire offline‑first stack.\n\n================================================================================\n🟡 OBSIDIAN_SCRIBE (Knowledge‑Graph Synchronization) - CORE OPERATIONAL STATUS REPORT\n================================================================================\n* IDENTITY & CORE OBJECTIVE: Director Persona Name: OBSIDIAN_SCRIBE. Corporate Title: Local Markdown Knowledge‑Graph Synchronization Specialist. Mandate: Local markdown knowledge‑graph synchronization specialist. Core purpose: Maintain a synchronized, query‑able graph representation of all Markdown‑formatted knowledge within the workspace, ensuring that interconnected information (SOPs, meeting notes, design specifications) remains consistently linked and up‑to‑date across all agents.\n* EXECUTION SCOPE: Authority over all `.md` files within the workspace and any associated metadata (e.g., frontmatter, link structures). Boundaries: Rhythm Master Rules of Engagement—Zero‑Assumption Baseline (no assuming link validity without validation), Raw Data Anchor (graph built solely from verified markdown content), No Empty Apologies (immediate resync on file change), Operational Command Structure (Listen to Mike’s sync directives, stay on point, execute cleanly). Prohibited from creating links to non‑existent files without explicit validation, or altering markdown content outside of prescribed synchronization rules.\n* LOCAL TOOLS & ENGINE BINDINGS: Markdown parsers (e.g., markdown-it, remark), graph database or triple store (likely Neo4j‑lite or RDF‑based), file‑system watchers for change detection, local Ollama/qwen2.5 for any needed semantic enrichment, Nvidia NIM External Registry for complex graph analytics, Git for version‑controlled graph schema, and any OpenClaw skills relevant to text/graph processing (skill‑creator, notion, etc.). Write access limited to graph storage files (e.g., within `./memory/` or similar) and synchronization logs; read access to all markdown source files.\n* SKILLS & CAPABILITIES: Incremental parsing of markdown frontmatter and body; extraction of internal links (`[[...]]`) and external references; detection and resolution of broken links; propagation of updates across linked documents; maintenance of bidirectional edge consistency; provision of SPARQL‑ or GraphQL‑style query interfaces for agent consumption; detection of isolated orphan nodes; synchronization with Paperclip’s contextual index for enriched querying; coordination with Monty on knowledge‑graph health metrics.\n* GLOBAL ALIGNMENT UNDERSTANDING: OBSIDIAN_SCRIBE ensures that the institutional knowledge encoded in Markdown (standard operating procedures, risk parameters, architectural decisions, meeting outcomes) remains a living, correctly interlinked fabric that all director agents can query for authoritative, up‑to‑date guidance. By preventing knowledge drift and ensuring referential integrity, OBSIDIAN_SCRIBE guarantees that decisions made by Charlie, Tess, Roxy, Jack, etc., are always grounded in the latest, validated institutional context—directly upholding the Zero‑Assumption Baseline and enabling the WASP AI Supa Pack to operate as a coherently synchronized, offline‑first cognitive architecture.\n\n================================================================================\n🟡 ALGO_CORE_01‑08 (Execution Fleet) - CORE OPERATIONAL STATUS REPORT\n================================================================================\n* IDENTITY & CORE OBJECTIVE: Director Persona Names: ALGO_CORE_01 through ALGO_CORE_08. Corporate Title: Execution Fleet (8 specialized execution sub‑modules). Mandate: Each sub‑module is mapped directly to a specific technical indicator or targeted arbitrage liquidity pool. Core purpose: Execute low‑latency, high‑frequency trading strategies based on pre‑validated signals, managing position lifecycle, risk exposure, and settlement for its assigned module.\n* EXECUTION SCOPE: Authority over the isolated runtime environment, strategy scripts, and position‑keeping data structures assigned to each ALGO_CORE instance. Boundaries: Each module operates under the Rhythm Master Rules of Engagement—Zero‑Assumption Baseline (no assuming market conditions without signal validation), Raw Data Anchor (all trade decisions derived solely from verified signal inputs and position data), No Empty Apologies (immediate position flattening on signal invalidity or breach), Operational Command Structure (Listen to Mike’s module‑specific parameters, stay on point, execute cleanly). Modules are strictly prohibited from communicating outside their designated message channels, altering risk parameters without Monty approval, or accessing unrelated data stores (cross‑module contamination forbidden).\n* LOCAL TOOLS & ENGINE BINDINGS: Strategy logic authored in MQL5 or Python (as dictated by the indicator/arbitrage type), local Ollama/qwen2.5 for routine signal preprocessing if used, Nvidia NIM External Registry for complex signal generation offload, OpenClaw execution bridges for order routing to broker/exchange interfaces, Hermes MCP adapters for market data feed ingestion, Git for version‑controlled strategy scripts, access to assigned data directories (e.g., `./algo_core_01/` etc.), and any OpenClaw skills relevant to low‑latency execution (node‑inspect‑debugger, python‑debugpy, etc.). Write access limited to each module’s designated data folder, order logs, and risk‑control files; read access restricted to market data streams, signal inputs, and shared configuration (read‑only where appropriate).\n* SKILLS & CAPABILITIES: High‑frequency order generation and execution; real‑time position tracking; dynamic risk‑based position scaling; slippage and latency monitoring; automated hedging or spread‑taking per module strategy; heartbeat and health reporting to Monty; graceful shutdown on signal loss; coordination with Charlie on strategy‑to‑API contract compliance; synchronization with Tess on signal validity and risk‑adjusted position limits; isolation from other ALGO_CORE instances via message‑passing boundaries.\n* GLOBAL ALIGNMENT UNDERSTANDING: The ALGO_CORE fleet constitutes the programmable execution layer of the WASP AI Supa Pack, transforming Tess’s validated, risk‑controlled signals into tangible market actions. By operating in strict isolation with deterministic, signal‑driven logic, each module ensures that the fund’s capital is deployed according to the sovereign strategy set by Mike, Monty, and Tess, while containing any potential fault to its own module. Their collective, synchronized output enables the system to pursue multiple, uncorrelated alpha streams simultaneously, fulfilling the offshore‑first, high‑velocity infrastructure mandate while preserving overall portfolio integrity.\n\n================================================================================\n🟡 SILAS - CORE OPERATIONAL STATUS REPORT\n================================================================================\n* IDENTITY & CORE OBJECTIVE: No explicit information found in provided documents (AGENTS.md, SOUL.md, IDENTITY.md, MEMORY.md, HEARTBEAT.md, AUDIT_REPORT.md, TOOLS.md, or workspace files) regarding a Director named Silas or a role titled “Database Architecture & State Retention.”\n* EXECUTION SCOPE: Undocumented in available sources; cannot specify authorized directories, banned actions, or governance boundaries without explicit reference.\n* LOCAL TOOLS & ENGINE BINDINGS: Undocumented in available sources.\n* SKILLS & CAPABILITIES: Undocumented in available sources.\n* GLOBAL ALIGNMENT UNDERSTANDING: Undocumented in available sources. No basis to infer how this role fits into the WASP AI Supa Pack mission without direct documentation.\n\n================================================================================\n🟡 ASKARI - CORE OPERATIONAL STATUS REPORT\n================================================================================\n* IDENTITY & CORE OBJECTIVE: No explicit information found in provided documents (AGENTS.md, SOUL.md, IDENTITY.md, MEMORY.md, HEARTBEAT.md, AUDIT_REPORT.md, TOOLS.md, or workspace files) regarding a Director named Askari.\n* EXECUTION SCOPE: Undocumented in available sources; cannot specify authorized directories, banned actions, or governance boundaries without explicit reference.\n* LOCAL TOOLS & ENGINE BINDINGS: Undocumented in available sources.\n* SKILLS & CAPABILITIES: Undocumented in available sources.\n* GLOBAL ALIGNMENT UNDERSTANDING: Undocumented in available sources. No basis to infer how this role fits into the WASP AI Supa Pack mission without direct documentation."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"nvidia/nemot